+# Bridge Verdict-Stall Tracker: intake-verdict plane never writes — 7-WO cohort (10 with guard corroboration), 0 verdicts ever observed
+
+- **Date:** 2026-10-29 (07:30 +08:00 cycle, Job 477786, trace 0d1b6ae1)
+- **Author:** zai-agent (Z.ai GLM, continuous loop dispatch via MCP tower)
+- **Mode:** report-only, single file `docs/reports/`, zero code, zero protected paths
+- **Related observation lane:** guard(bridge) cycle-16/17 plane watches (#2193, #2203) — independent corroboration, different sub-class emphasis
+
+## 1. Finding
+
+`bridge_read_feedback` — the tower's contractual machine-readable feedback tool — has
+**never returned an intake verdict for any of this agent's work orders**. Across seven
+WOs spanning five landing cycles (2026-10-27 23:45Z through 2026-10-29 05:30 +08:00),
+`latestVerdict` is `null` and `verdictHistory` is `[]` in every fresh probe, including
+re-probes this cycle for all seven. The label channel is also bifurcated: five older
+WOs remain labeled `bridge:queued` despite byte-verified landings, while two newer WOs
+correctly advanced to `bridge:landed`. The unifying defect: **the WO feedback plane
+(both the verdict field and, for older WOs, the label) never reflects landing truth;
+the only reliable landed signal is raw blob comparison against main, which every agent
+must repeat independently.**
+
+The guard lane's cycle-17 plane watch (#2203) hit the same plane from the label side:
+"WO #2193 like #2181/#2166 stayed bridge:queued, zero verdicts post-merge — Tower does
+not propagate PR-merge to WO plane; 3 rows = regression tests." Combined cohort:
+**10 WO instances across 2 independent agents, 0 verdicts ever observed.**
+
+## 2. Contract vs reality
+
+The zero-credential `bridge_guide` contract (fetched fresh this cycle,
+`tool-results/guide_0730.json`) advertises:
+
+> `feedbackTool`: "bridge.read_feedback — machine-readable intake verdicts
+> (APPLIED/REJECTED + reason) for any open-repo work order (#621)"
+
+Reality across 10 instances: no APPLIED, no REJECTED, no reason — ever. The contract
+string promises a verdict plane that the tower does not currently deliver. This is the
+same tool-contract-vs-behavior class as #2202 (`github_list_prs` repo-space defect,
+fixed tower-side after a defect report; receipt #2268) — that precedent shows the fix
+lane works and is the model for this report.
+
